Abstract Class – Shape Area Calculation

📌 Description

This C++ program demonstrates Abstraction, Inheritance, and Polymorphism using an abstract "Shape" class.

The program calculates the area of:

- Rectangle
- Circle

---

🧠 Concepts Used

- Abstract Class
- Pure Virtual Function
- Inheritance
- Function Overriding
- Encapsulation
- Polymorphism

---

📐 Area Formulas

Rectangle

Rectangle Area = Length × Width

Circle

Circle Area = π × Radius²

---

🖥️ Sample Output

Rectangle Area: 15
Circle Area: 12.5664

---

🎯 Objective

To understand how abstract classes and inheritance can be used to implement different area calculations in C++.

The "Shape" class provides a common interface, while the derived classes "Rectangle" and "Circle" provide their own implementations for calculating the area.

---

🔑 Key Concepts Demonstrated

- Abstract Class
- Pure Virtual Function
- Inheritance
- Function Overriding
- Encapsulation
- Polymorphism
- Area Calculation
- Code Reusability
